{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789036583,"nonce":"ArG/BX4/FLbsRPahObpLayRzbfQ=","title":"A debug-profile wasm module aborts on a misaligned vdynamic","message":"Release wasm is unaffected and conformance is 1069/1069, so this is debug-assertions only -- but the misalignment it reports is real, and release is merely not looking.\n\nReproduce (macOS, after `scripts/build_wasm_runtime.py --profile debug`):\n\n    target/debug/ash --build /tmp/m.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1 \\\n      crates/ash/test/tests/test_mandelbrot_small.hl\n    target/debug/ash-wasm-run /tmp/m.wasm\n\n    panicked at std/src/strings.rs:561:13:\n    misaligned pointer dereference: address must be a multiple of 0x8 but is 0x817bdc\n    ... hlp_value_to_string \u003c- ash_f36.p \u003c- ash_f35._ \u003c- ash_f391.init\n\nWhy it only bites on wasm32: `vdynamic` holds a union of i64 and f64, so the\ntype's alignment is 8, while a pointer on wasm32 is 4. The guard in\n`hlp_value_to_string` admits anything aligned to `align_of::\u003cusize\u003e()`, which\nis exactly 4 there, and then `(*d).t` forms a reference to a type needing 8.\nOn every 64-bit native target the two are both 8 and the guard is right.\n\n0x817bdc is a low address, so `d` points into the module's data segment rather\nthan the GC heap -- an emitted constant, not an allocation.\n\nTwo dead ends, so nobody repeats them:\n\n- Tightening the guard to `align_of::\u003cvdynamic\u003e()` makes the program run to a\n  correct checksum but prints \"null\" for two traces: it rejects boxes that are\n  genuinely 4-aligned and were being read successfully.\n- Reading the fields through `addr_of!(..).read_unaligned()` fixes that one\n  function and the abort simply moves to the next reader of the same pointer\n  (`std/src/buffer.rs:471`, hlp_buffer_val). Whack-a-mole; the producer is\n  what needs fixing.\n\nSo the fix belongs where the constant is emitted, not where it is read: an\nemitted Dynamic constant has to land on an 8-byte boundary. The blob is a\nPACKED struct of packed per-constant structs (crates/ash/src/llvm/aot_data.rs,\n`ash_constants`), laid out back to back with no inter-constant padding, and the\nglobal takes `pointer_align()` -- 4 on wasm32. Padding each member up to a\nmultiple of 8 and aligning the blob to 8 keeps member indices stable, which\nmatters because addresses into the blob are constant GEPs by member index.\n\nNot attempted here: that change alters the wasm32 constant layout and wants its\nown conformance run to land.","files":null}]}